{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 9,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.089,
            0.454,
            0.104
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Example 11.4"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.306,
            0.105,
            0.9,
            0.172
          ],
          "content": "**The potential difference between the terminals of an electric heater is 60 V when it draws a current of 4 A from the source. What current will the heater draw if the potential difference is increased to 120 V? Solution**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.172,
            0.828,
            0.189
          ],
          "content": "We are given, potential difference $V = 6 0   \\mathrm { V } ,$ current $I   =   4   \\mathrm { A }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.196,
            0.726,
            0.229
          ],
          "content": "**According to Ohm’s law,** $R=\\frac{V}{I}=\\frac{60\\  V }{4\\  A }=15\\ \\Omega$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.306,
            0.233,
            0.899,
            0.267
          ],
          "content": "**When the potential difference is increased to 120 V the current is given by**"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.272,
            0.556,
            0.307
          ],
          "content": "{ \\mathrm { c u r r e n t } } = { \\frac { V } { R } } = { \\frac { 1 2 0 { \\mathrm { ~ V ~ } } } { 1 5 \\; \\Omega } } = 8 { \\mathrm { ~ A ~ } } .",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.313,
            0.708,
            0.331
          ],
          "content": "**The current through the heater becomes 8 A.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.308,
            0.344,
            0.454,
            0.36
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Example 11.5"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.306,
            0.359,
            0.9,
            0.426
          ],
          "content": "**Resistance of a metal wire of length 1 m is 26** Ω **at** $2 0 ^ { \\circ } \\mathbb { C }$ **. If the diameter of the wire is 0.3 mm, what will be the resistivity of the metal at that temperature? Using Table 11.2, predict the material of the wire.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.429,
            0.401,
            0.444
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Solution"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.306,
            0.445,
            0.899,
            0.478
          ],
          "content": "**We are given the resistance R of the** $\\mathrm{wire}=26\\ \\Omega$ **, the diameter** $d = 0.3\\  mm  = 3 \\times 10^{-4}$ **m, and the length l of the wire = 1 m.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.306,
            0.478,
            0.899,
            0.516
          ],
          "content": "**Therefore, from Eq. (11.10), the resistivity of the given metallic wire is** $\\rho \\quad = \\quad ( R A / l ) \\quad \\equiv \\quad ( R \\pi d ^ { 2 } / 4 l )$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.519,
            0.618,
            0.537
          ],
          "content": "**Substitution of values in this gives**"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.539,
            0.504,
            0.556
          ],
          "content": "\\rho = 1.84 \\times 10^{-6}   \\Omega    m",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_13.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.306,
            0.559,
            0.898,
            0.595
          ],
          "content": "**The resistivity of the metal at** $2 0 ^ { \\circ } \\mathbf { C }$ **is** $1 . 8 4 \\: \\times \\: 1 0 ^ { - 6 } \\Omega$ **m**. From **Table 11.2, we see that this is the resistivity of manganese.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.608,
            0.454,
            0.623
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Example 11.6"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.623,
            0.9,
            0.691
          ],
          "content": "**A wire of given material having length l and area of cross-section A has a resistance of 4** Ω. **What would be the resistance of another wire of the same material having length l/2 and area of cross-section 2A? Solution**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.308,
            0.693,
            0.427,
            0.709
          ],
          "content": "**For first wire**"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.312,
            0.715,
            0.474,
            0.747
          ],
          "content": "R_{1} = \\rho \\frac{l}{A} = 4\\Omega",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_18.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.311,
            0.749,
            0.495,
            0.767
          ],
          "content": "**Now for second wire**"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.312,
            0.772,
            0.546,
            0.808
          ],
          "content": "R_{2} = \\rho \\frac{l/2}{2A} = \\frac{1}{4} \\rho \\frac{l}{A}",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_20.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.312,
            0.814,
            0.449,
            0.845
          ],
          "content": "R _ { _ 2 } = \\frac { 1 } { 4 } \\quad R _ { _ L }",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_21.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.312,
            0.848,
            0.384,
            0.867
          ],
          "content": "R _ { 2 } { = } 1 \\Omega",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_22.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.311,
            0.869,
            0.634,
            0.886
          ],
          "content": "**The resistance of the new wire is 1**Ω."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.831,
            0.916,
            0.9,
            0.93
          ],
          "content": "**Science**"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.091,
